<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35868" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔννοια</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοῦς</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>act of thinking, reflection, cogitation</i> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συντονία διανοίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Def.</u>
					414a
				</span></i>
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄξιον ἐννοίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					657a
				</span></i>
			,al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>notion, conception,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρόνου ἔννοια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					47a
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ταῖς περὶ τὸ ὂν . . ἐννοίαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Phlb.</u>
					59d
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. λαβεῖν</span> to form <i>an
				idea,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴσθησιν λαβεῖν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				73c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ καλοῦ ἔ. ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1179b15
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐννοίας χάριν λέγειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Metaph.</u>
					1073b12
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔννοιαι,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαντασίαι, αἰσθήσεις,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>MA</u>
				701b17
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ ἀθρόαν ἔ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					1p.23U.
				</span></i>
			 (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ πᾶσαν ἔ. θυμοῦ</span>
			every <i>kind, variety</i> of anger, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Ir.</u>
				p.90
			</span></i> W.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοξαστικαὶ ἔ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Sent.</u>
					24
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ἔ. ἔρχεσθαί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					1.57.4
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ἔ. τινὸς ἄγειν
			τινά</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				49.10
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ κοινὴ ἔ.</span> the common
				<i>notion,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				10.27.8
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοιναὶ ἔ.</span>
			<i>axioms,</i> heading in <i><span class="en">
				Euc.
			</span></i>; general <i>ideas,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Chrysipp.Stoic.
				2.154
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψιλὴ ἔ.</span> mere, i.e.
			vague, <i>notion,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Simp.
				<u>in Ph.</u>
				18.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>intent,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				1026
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔννοιαν λαβεῖν</span> form
				<i>a design,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				1027
			</span></i>; <i>intention</i> of a testator, <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				1.13
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. ἔχειν περί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					769e
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. ἐμποιεῖν</span> put an
				<i>idea</i> into one's head, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				5.150
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. ἐμπίπτει τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					3.1.13
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>good sense, better judgement,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρὰ τὴν ἔννοιαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.1077d
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>sense</i> of a word, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				69.21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> Rhet.,
				<i>thought,</i> opp. <i>diction</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέξις</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Id.</u>
				2.4
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Prog.</u>
				6
			</span></i>.</div>
